  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "The parts are the same as in step 1, with no additions or removals.",
   "The accelerometer's six pins sit in neighbouring columns 10-15 of the top half of the breadboard, in row a, in the card's pin order (ST, Z, Y, X, GND, VCC). Each jumper wire goes in row b of the same column, so it shares a strip with its accelerometer pin.",
   "Pin table: ST to A0, Z to A1, Y to A2, X to A3, GND to A4, VDD to A5. A4 is driven LOW as ground and A5 HIGH as 5 V by the sketch (D18 and D19), so no 5V or GND pin is used.",
   "The captured circuit image was cut off. The six-wire layout and the wire colours (black and red in particular) are assumed from the pin table.",
   "Some ADXL3xx boards are 3.3 V only, and the tutorial warns about this. The catalogue's adxl335 card gives no supply range, so I kept the tutorial's 5 V wiring."
  ]
 },
